## Scope

The root LICENSE applies to original OpenArc work. It uses the BSD-3-Clause
license text published by the Open Source Initiative:
https://opensource.org/license/bsd-3-clause

Chromium and its dependencies keep their own licenses. OpenArc's license does
not replace notices in upstream files, patch context, dependencies, or generated
artifacts. Upstream source is fetched separately using the pinned build inputs.
Preserve the license files in that source tree.

This is an initial source-repository attribution inventory. It is not a complete
notice bundle for a browser binary, and it does not assert that every fetched or
transitive dependency has been audited. No qualified release binary is supplied
by this initial scaffold. Before distributing a binary, assemble and verify
notices for the exact source revision, build configuration, resources, and
libraries actually included; see docs/RELEASING.md.

